<custom_item>
  type        : CONFIG_CHECK_NOT
  description : "OS10-RTR-001020 - The Dell OS10 Router must be configured to advertise a hop limit of at least 32 in Router Advertisement messages for IPv6 stateless auto-configuration deployments."
  info        : "The Neighbor Discovery protocol allows a hop limit value to be advertised by routers in a Router Advertisement message being used by hosts instead of the standardized default value. If a very small value was configured and advertised to hosts on the LAN segment, communications would fail due to the hop limit reaching zero before the packets sent by a host reached its destination."
  solution    : "Configure each IPv6 interface to advertise a hop limit of at least 32 in Router Advertisement messages as in the example below.

OS10(config)# interface ethernet 1/1/4
OS10(conf-if-eth1/1/4)# ipv6 nd send-ra
OS10(conf-if-eth1/1/4)# ipv6 nd hop-limit 32"
  reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|Dell_OS10_Switch_Router_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-269902r1052091_rule,STIG-ID|OS10-RTR-001020,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-269902"
